## Gaps in the literature and RESA's contribution

Comparison with similar studies revealed the gaps listed below. The badge on each item shows whether the gap has been confirmed or is already partly filled.


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}

```{=html}
<ul class="lista-lacunas">
<li>
<span class="selo-lacuna lacuna-confirmada">confirmed</span>
<b>1. </b>
There is no viability study of AFS or productive restoration in a settlement in Mato Grosso.
</li>
<li>
<span class="selo-lacuna lacuna-confirmada">confirmed</span>
<b>2. </b>
There is no study of this kind in the Pantanal.
</li>
<li>
<span class="selo-lacuna lacuna-parcial">partly filled</span>
<b>3. </b>
Valuing carbon at market prices in settlements has been addressed only in part, in analogous studies from other countries and in studies without a sample of families.
</li>
<li>
<span class="selo-lacuna lacuna-confirmada">confirmed</span>
<b>4. </b>
No single study integrates differences between families, PES, carbon and risk.
</li>
</ul>
```

